  "verification": "Counts match the wiki's own statements on the retrieval date (44 killers, 54 survivors, 21 realms, 46 maps). Names are the wiki's English page titles. The game does not always print the page title: an entry may carry 'aliases', on-screen spellings that map to the same id. An alias is listed only after it was seen in the game and records where in 'seenOnScreen'; so far one is known (survivor 'Leon S. Kennedy' for 'Leon Scott Kennedy', 2026-10-24, owner screenshot). Whether other names are printed differently is UNKNOWN until seen. An entry's own 'seenOnScreen' means its name was read from the game screen; an entry without it has not yet been seen on screen. 'eventModes' holds limited-time event names (read from the second line of the PLAY EVENT header) and is expected to grow; only 'Haunted by Daylight' (seen 2026-10-24) is listed, and it is not on the wiki's Game Modes page. 'resultOutcomes' holds the result-screen texts: 'Escaped' was seen on screen on 2026-10-24; 'Sacrificed', 'Dead' and the four killer results are taken from the wiki's Tally Screen page (Match Result section) and are NOT yet seen on screen, so their on-screen wording is UNKNOWN. How each remaining name is rendered on screen in the game (casing, punctuation, line breaks) is UNKNOWN until checked against the owner's captures. The roster changes with every chapter, so this list is dated and must be refreshed; the wiki announces one further realm and map that is not yet released and is not listed. Every killer and survivor carries 'code', the game's character code (K for killers, S for survivors) that prefixes its portrait file names, for example K27_TheOnryo_Portrait.png in imported packs; codes are facts, not wiki content. Each code maps to one id and never changes; they were reviewed on 2026-10-24 (docs/evidence/s5b-0-spike.md section 4, with K06, K25 and S06 INFERRED) and equal tests/fixtures/roster/seed.json. The wiki's own portrait file names number some characters differently (K05/K06 and S18/S19 are swapped there), so wiki file names are not a source for codes.",
